  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197602",
      "title": "Setting Sizes Dynamically (for different Orientations)",
      "lectureOrder": 84,
      "videoOrder": 81,
      "sourceHash": "8804801108e7856fd053f5369e1c518f58e52d8bc2ece0cc061e882efcd7bb3a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 2.873,
          "en": "Now, what can we do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.873,
          "end": 4.76,
          "en": "about different orientations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.76,
          "end": 6.97,
          "en": "and this app looking better?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.97,
          "end": 10.757,
          "en": "Well, for one, we can again, use the dimensions API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.757,
          "end": 12.74,
          "en": "And we could, for example, take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.74,
          "end": 17.74,
          "en": "at the available height to base this margin to the top here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.35,
          "end": 20.61,
          "en": "on that available height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.61,
          "end": 23.99,
          "en": "so that we don't have as much of a margin to the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.99,
          "end": 27.833,
          "en": "if we have less height available on our device here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.698,
          "end": 32.81,
          "en": "Now for this, we can go to the start game screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.81,
          "end": 35.24,
          "en": "where we have this margin to the top here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.24,
          "end": 38.57,
          "en": "on this view with the root container style,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.57,
          "end": 41.4,
          "en": "there, we have this hard-coded value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.4,
          "end": 44.12,
          "en": "And as you learn with the image on the game over screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.12,
          "end": 46.803,
          "en": "hard-coded values aren't that great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 49.49,
          "en": "And therefore, in start game screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.49,
          "end": 52.34,
          "en": "we can of course, import the dimensions API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.34,
          "end": 54.435,
          "en": "from React Native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.435,
          "end": 58.023,
          "en": "And then use that to change that margin to the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.89,
          "end": 61.68,
          "en": "So now we could get the device height here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.68,
          "end": 66.67,
          "en": "instead of the device width by using dimensions get window",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.67,
          "end": 68.173,
          "en": "and now the height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.05,
          "end": 70.53,
          "en": "And then here we could, again, check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.53,
          "end": 71.76,
          "en": "if the (indistinct) height",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.76,
          "end": 76.357,
          "en": "is maybe, let's say, smaller than 400.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.22,
          "end": 82.53999999999999,
          "en": "And in that case, we want to set a margin to the top of 30",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.53999999999999,
          "end": 84.88,
          "en": "and otherwise 100.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.88,
          "end": 87.1,
          "en": "And you will have to play around with that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.1,
          "end": 90.57,
          "en": "to find out what looks good and what works well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.57,
          "end": 93.78,
          "en": "But if we save this, now we have less margin to the top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.78,
          "end": 95.55,
          "en": "if we are in landscape mode.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.55,
          "end": 97.706,
          "en": "on both iOS and Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.706,
          "end": 102.47800000000001,
          "en": "And we could go for 380, since that was our width before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.47800000000001,
          "end": 106.19,
          "en": "If we rotate the device, that is our height break point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.19,
          "end": 108.231,
          "en": "that sets these two devices apart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.231,
          "end": 111.41,
          "en": "to still have the bigger margin here on iOS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.41,
          "end": 113.991,
          "en": "and the smaller margin on Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.991,
          "end": 118.53,
          "en": "Now, it is totally up to you how much margin you wanna have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.53,
          "end": 120.493,
          "en": "but this would be one way of doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.43,
          "end": 125.21,
          "en": "But even with that solution, it's still not perfect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.21,
          "end": 128.19,
          "en": "What if a user changes the orientation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.19,
          "end": 131.08,
          "en": "whilst he or she is using this app?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.08,
          "end": 132.79,
          "en": "If we switch back to portrait,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.79,
          "end": 135.61,
          "en": "now we have that smaller margin still.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.61,
          "end": 138.07,
          "en": "And the same, of course, on iOS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.07,
          "end": 140.38,
          "en": "it just left my screen for a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.38,
          "end": 141.99,
          "en": "And the same would be true for iOS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.99,
          "end": 144.42000000000002,
          "en": "if you would switch back, but there, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.42000000000002,
          "end": 145.91,
          "en": "thanks to this break point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.91,
          "end": 148.143,
          "en": "the margin was bigger anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.19,
          "end": 150.7,
          "en": "But you can see it on Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.7,
          "end": 152.43,
          "en": "If we have that smaller margin",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 154.51,
          "en": "because we start in landscape mode,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.51,
          "end": 157.72,
          "en": "then we keep it even if we rotate back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.72,
          "end": 160.18,
          "en": "Because that is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 160.18,
          "end": 165.04,
          "en": "This code here, where we get the device height and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 165.04,
          "end": 167.31,
          "en": "is only executed once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.31,
          "end": 170.89,
          "en": "when this component code, this entire file code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.89,
          "end": 174.223,
          "en": "is parsed and executed for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.11,
          "end": 177.692,
          "en": "So if we adjust the screen orientation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 177.692,
          "end": 180.01,
          "en": "after starting this game,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.01,
          "end": 183.122,
          "en": "this code down here will not get executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.122,
          "end": 187.65,
          "en": "Yes, the component file, this file will execute again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 187.65,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "from time to time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 191.53,
          "en": "For example, when our estate changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.53,
          "end": 194.56,
          "en": "But the code outside of this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 194.56,
          "end": 197.43,
          "en": "will not be executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.43,
          "end": 200.8,
          "en": "So therefore, if it's possible to switch the orientation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.8,
          "end": 204.15800000000002,
          "en": "whilst using this game or this app in general,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.15800000000002,
          "end": 208.26,
          "en": "then you might not wanna use the dimensions API like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.26,
          "end": 211.91,
          "en": "You could, but you then might be locking in values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 211.91,
          "end": 214.163,
          "en": "that you don't really want thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.35,
          "end": 218.3,
          "en": "What you should do instead, is you should write this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.3,
          "end": 220.27,
          "en": "in a more responsive way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.27,
          "end": 224.28,
          "en": "which adjusts to changing device orientations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 224.28,
          "end": 228.42000000000002,
          "en": "And thankfully, this is all the very simple and easy to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.42000000000002,
          "end": 230.37,
          "en": "with React Native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.37,
          "end": 233.4,
          "en": "Instead of locking in the device height here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 233.4,
          "end": 236.204,
          "en": "and instead of setting the margin top here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 236.204,
          "end": 239.23,
          "en": "what you should do, is move that code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.23,
          "end": 241.15,
          "en": "into your component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.15,
          "end": 244.42,
          "en": "So any code that should react to device orientation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 244.42,
          "end": 248.04,
          "en": "or size changes, should go into the component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 248.04,
          "end": 251.81,
          "en": "because this function, unlike the overall file code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 251.81,
          "end": 254.103,
          "en": "will get executed multiple times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 255.155,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "Now, React Native gives you an alternative way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 262.81,
          "en": "of accessing the dimensions API, which allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.81,
          "end": 266.7,
          "en": "to then react to device size or dimension changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 266.7,
          "end": 268.563,
          "en": "inside of component functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 269.44,
          "end": 272.12,
          "en": "React Native gives you a hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 272.12,
          "end": 275.793,
          "en": "the use Window dimensions hook, which you can use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.04,
          "end": 279.5,
          "en": "Now, like all React hooks, you have to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.5,
          "end": 284.38,
          "en": "inside of a component function or inside another hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 284.38,
          "end": 286.431,
          "en": "And you then simply call this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.431,
          "end": 288.83,
          "en": "to get back an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 288.83,
          "end": 291.4,
          "en": "on which you can use object de-structuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.4,
          "end": 293.823,
          "en": "to get the width and height Of the device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.28,
          "end": 296.93,
          "en": "So now here, we get width and height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 296.93,
          "end": 301.93,
          "en": "but internally, this hook will watch the device dimensions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.61,
          "end": 304.58,
          "en": "And whenever they change, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.58,
          "end": 307.35,
          "en": "because the device ice gets rotated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.35,
          "end": 310.46,
          "en": "this component function will get executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.46,
          "end": 313.473,
          "en": "and we will get an updated width and height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.31,
          "end": 316.51,
          "en": "And that means that now we can derive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 316.51,
          "end": 320.1,
          "en": "our margin top dynamically inside of this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 320.1,
          "end": 322.64,
          "en": "based on this dynamic height or width,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 322.64,
          "end": 325.023,
          "en": "and then use this in our JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 325.97,
          "end": 329.35,
          "en": "So maybe here, right before returning JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 329.35,
          "end": 331.577,
          "en": "we could get our margin top",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 331.577,
          "end": 334.254,
          "en": "by simply using height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.254,
          "end": 337.402,
          "en": "And then the same logic as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 337.402,
          "end": 340.77,
          "en": "where we have this check here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 340.77,
          "end": 344.279,
          "en": "to then set a margin top of 30 or 100.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 344.279,
          "end": 346.161,
          "en": "But we now do this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 346.161,
          "end": 351.058,
          "en": "in our component function, right before we return JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 351.058,
          "end": 354.05,
          "en": "And now we just need to make sure that this value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 354.05,
          "end": 355.98,
          "en": "gets applied.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 355.98,
          "end": 358.02,
          "en": "So here I'll name it, margin top distance,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 358.02,
          "end": 359.37,
          "en": "but this name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 360.43,
          "end": 363.89,
          "en": "So that means that we now wanna merge this dynamic style",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 363.89,
          "end": 366.56,
          "en": "into our style sheet object that we're setting here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 366.56,
          "end": 368.13,
          "en": "on the view.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 368.13,
          "end": 369.95,
          "en": "And thankfully, as you learned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 369.95,
          "end": 371.93,
          "en": "merging styles is simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 371.93,
          "end": 374.75,
          "en": "You could, for example, turn this into an array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 374.75,
          "end": 377.56,
          "en": "and then add another style object like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 377.56,
          "end": 382.03,
          "en": "where you set margin top equal to the margin top distance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 382.03,
          "end": 383.293,
          "en": "that is derived here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.32,
          "end": 387.14,
          "en": "And since this component function will now re-execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 387.14,
          "end": 388.98,
          "en": "whenever the dimensions change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 388.98,
          "end": 392.793,
          "en": "this will adjust whenever the device orientation changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 394.36,
          "end": 396.51,
          "en": "So now with that, if we save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 396.51,
          "end": 399.04,
          "en": "and we force a reload on all devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 399.04,
          "end": 402.84000000000003,
          "en": "Here, we start with a lot of margin to the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
